-- title:
--   No varpi-torsion in the Cartier module of a special formal mathcal O_D-module
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be prime and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$; write $\mathbb Z_{p^2}=W(\mathbb F_{p^2})$ for the coefficient ring `Zp2 p`, and let $\iota\colon \mathbb Z_{p^2}\to W(k)$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $B=W(k)/pW(k)$ (the quotient by the ideal generated by $p$) and let $\Phi$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $B$: a two-dimensional commutative formal group law $\Phi.F$ over $B$ together with series $\mathrm{act}(a)$ for $a\in\mathbb Z_{p^2}$ and a series $\varpi$, all endomorphisms of the law, with $\mathrm{act}$ a ring action (unital, multiplicative for composition, additive for addition via the group law) and $\varpi\circ\varpi=\mathrm{act}(p)$, $\varpi\circ\mathrm{act}(a)=\mathrm{act}(\sigma a)\circ\varpi$ for the Witt-vector Frobenius $\sigma$. Assume $\Phi$ is special with respect to $j=\iota$ followed by reduction modulo $p$, that is, the tangent pieces $\Phi.\mathrm{lieZero}(j)$ and $\Phi.\mathrm{lieOne}(j)$ are complementary submodules and each is an invertible $B$-module, and that $\Phi$ has height $4$, i.e. $\mathrm{act}(p)$ has kernel of degree $p^4$. Then for every element $m$ of the Cartier module of $\Phi.F$ (a tuple of power series in countably many variables, with zero constant term, additive for the Witt addition law), $\varpi$ acting on $m$ through the induced additive endomorphism `endAct Φ.varpiEnd` and giving $0$ forces $m=0$.
--
--   This is the torsion-freeness statement for the Cartier module $M=\operatorname{Hom}(\widehat W,\Phi)$ of a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module of height $4$ over $W(k)/p$: multiplication by the uniformiser $\varpi$ of the quaternion order is injective on $M$, hence, since $\varpi^2=p$, so is multiplication by $p$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the argument, in the analysis of the $\eta$-pieces and of the rigidified centraliser action on Cartier modules.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_eq_zero_of_endAct_varpiEnd_eq_zero_of_isSpecial_of_hasHeight.lean

